## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates understanding of practical CORS security fixes, including origin whitelisting, credentials handling, and preflight validation in production applications.

## Key Concepts

- CORS and the ACAO header behavior with wildcards
- Access-Control-Allow-Credentials and the Vary: Origin header
- Preflight OPTIONS request handling
- Authentication boundaries and data exposure risks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Express middleware
const ALLOWED_ORIGIN = 'https://app.example.com';

app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const origin = req.headers.origin;

  if (origin === ALLOWED_ORIGIN) {
    res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', ALLOWED_ORIGIN);
    res.setHeader('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials', 'true');
    res.setHeader('Vary', 'Origin');
  }

  if (req.method === 'OPTIONS') {
    return res.send(204);
  }

  next();
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

Beginner security tasks often miss logs containing PII. This question tests practical, actionable steps to prevent leakage without disrupting features.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation in logs
- PII redaction and masking
- Centralized, encrypted log sinks
- Least-privilege log access and audit trails
- CI validation for log content

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: redactPII function for logs
function redactPII(record){
  const masked = {...record};
  if (masked.email) masked.email = masked.email.replace(/[^@]+@/,'***@');
  if (masked.phone) masked.phone = masked.phone.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g,'*');
  return masked;
}
```

